{"id": "EUVD-2026-86876", "enisaUuid": "0058e887-b164-3a16-8821-d65fa99373ac", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmptcp: syncookies: remember the request backup flag\n\nInstead of using an uninitialised bit when copying the info in\nsubflow_ulp_clone().\n\nTo fix this, no need to extend the join_entry structure: backup is\ncoming from struct mptcp_subflow_request_sock, only one bit. Do the same\nhere by using one bit for both.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:21:54", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:09:31", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c97fa2c7ada82d4cac1c6c00643238dc4c462f15", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1668b34452009d27be3262646de748a3e48ffd51", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b138e7dc719f0a3949de8bb6500b8cf1604eea06", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/360d99258a6402cb8e49771460944f19f04d25b7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/61178d0b85b4b1b53e78b06e89d018d22d102f88", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/00b2bd518911e0daab00f4749cce68c191ccebb4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/06d649f9cd03a9f8e768a658b20acf8d2c8022e0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b76c0e28b392620dfbaf92cdeedbf115820b44cb"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97568", "GHSA-6cg2-hrxf-655w"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0fa050df-b392-30df-a341-b69244f9496f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "73e2baa301ee3f62ff971e68877adeb37f98cc67"}, {"id": "127992d8-6b5f-30f4-bbf5-9500acd206e6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.10.224 <5.10.271"}, {"id": "128abb96-d201-3867-ba7a-7fec41cb3eb5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "1e17d478-4d50-3d49-953e-02905b2a1524", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1008f2bcbc8e461c1df3aebba30ac4f616ebe570 <c97fa2c7ada82d4cac1c6c00643238dc4c462f15"}, {"id": "28aa6